lue flame lights and the counter climbs to 1950"},"do":[{"p":"stove","v":"lightB","w":"blue"},{"p":"stove","v":"warm","w":"blue","o":0.3},{"p":"temp","v":"count","w":"blue","d":2.4}],"shots":[{"focus":["temp","stove"],"width":0.94}]},{"s":"finish","shows":{"p":"stove","does":"a grate and a pot appear over the blue flame and the spark ticks"},"do":[{"p":"temp","v":"hide","w":"Add"},{"p":"stove","v":"grate","w":"grate"},{"p":"stove","v":"pot","w":"pot"},{"p":"stove","v":"sparks","w":"spark","o":-0.7}],"shots":[{"focus":["stove"],"width":0.85}]},{"s":"congrats","shows":{"p":"stove","does":"a calm blue flame burns under the pot"},"do":[{"p":"stove","v":"sparksBack"}],"shots":[{"focus":"home"}]}],"audio":{"cards":[{"text":"25 MILLIVOLTS","at":{"s":"fix2","w":"25"},"d":1.6},{"text":"1950 °C","at":{"s":"mythFact","w":"1950"},"d":1.8}],"sfx":[{"lib":"flame","at":{"s":"hook","w":"light","o":0.4},"d":1.2},{"lib":"flame","at":{"s":"fix1","w":"blue"},"d":1.2},{"lib":"water_rush","at":{"s":"problem2","w":"gas"},"d":1.4},{"lib":"flame","at":{"s":"mythFact","w":"blue"},"d":1.2}],"chimes":[{"s":"name"},{"s":"fix2","w":"25"},{"s":"mythFact","w":"1950"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"codeShots":true,"why":"A gas stove is shown cut open in a kitchen. One gas line runs up to a jet, and a bare yellow flame turns into a blue Bunsen-style burner that draws in air. A probe and a safety plunger then stop a leak, and a grate and pot finish it. The camera opens close on the jet, moves to mid shots of the burner, and ends on the home view with the blue flame under a pot.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you let gas out of a pipe and light it, you have a stove."},{"role":"problem","text":"But the lazy yellow flame glows with unburnt soot, and black soot pours off it."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you add a burner tube with air holes, and the flame turns clean and blue."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a Bunsen burner."},{"role":"how","text":"Gas shoots up the tube and draws in about half of the air it needs through the holes."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But a draft can blow the flame out, and the gas keeps drifting into the room."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add a thermocouple that makes about 25 millivolts to hold a safety valve open, and the valve shuts when the flame dies."},{"role":"myth","text":"And a big yellow flame is not the hotter one, as people think."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"The blue flame is the hot one, reaching roughly 1,950 to 2,000 degrees Celsius."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a grate, a pot and a clicking spark igniter."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a gas stove."}]}